  "explanation": {
    "id": "b349aa1f-440f-4206-a445-fa84fead34d0",
    "body": "The video explanation of 11a is incorrect. The row reduction is fine but the solution should be \n\n$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\left[\\begin{array}{cccc} 3/2 \\\\ 13/2  \\\\ 1/2 \\\\1 \\end{array}\\right] t\n$\nThe nullspace is spanned by the spanning vector $ \\left[\\begin{array}{cccc} 3/2 \\\\ 13/2  \\\\ 1/2 \\\\1 \\end{array}\\right] $. \nThe zero vector is within the nullspace- it is obtained by multiplying the above spanning vector by a constant 0. \n\nThe nullspace is not a subspace of R3 because elements in the nullspace have 4 elements whereas elements in R3 only have 3. This does not make sense so a is incorrect. \n\nThe explanations for B, C, D, E still stand, just recognize that the expression I wrote for $\\mathbf{x}$ in the video is incorrect. \n\nSide note: The nullspace is a subspace of R4. It satisfies all the requirements (you can check the last two yourself): 1). includes 0 vector, 2). any two elements in the nullspace when added together yields an element still in the nullspace, 3). any element in the nullspace multiplied by a scalar is still an element in the nullspace. ",
    "questionId": "da251a6a-cde4-4a3c-8718-483e3a6186b5",
